[Possibly Estelle Emma Skidmore Doremus or her daugher, musician Estelle E. Doremus]</field><field name="scopecontent_teim">In Reference To: Friendship / Personal / Social; &#34;Collection of Mr. Barbon&#34; ; Mary Leila (Lilian) Horsford</field><field name="scopecontent_teim">8 Pages, Bound &amp; Unbound</field><field name="scopecontent_teim">Handwritten in Ink</field><field name="scopecontent_teim">Measurements: 4&#34; x 6&#34; - 4.5&#34; x 7&#34;</field><field name="scopecontent_teim">Estelle Emma Skidmore Doremus (May 6, 1830 – May 21, 1905) was the daughter of Hubbard Skidmore, who served in the American Revolutionary War, and became a charter member and honorary vice president general of the National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution (DAR). Estelle was also a charter officer and regent of the New York City chapter of the DAR (1892 - 1894). The wife of U.S. chemist Robert Ogden Doremus, Estelle was a leading member of the American community in Paris during the height of the Second French Empire. William Nelson&#39;s Genealogy of the Doremus Family is available through New York University Libraries via BobCat.</field><field name="series_si">Record Group IV: Horsford Family &gt;&gt; Series A: Eben Norton Horsford &gt;&gt; Subseries 1: Correspondence &gt;&gt; Subsubseries a: Academic and Family
